1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:03,220
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:03,860
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:08,600
My name is Catherine and we're going to be purchasing some wine today, right Marco?

4
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:09,240
That's right.

5
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:15,580
Today we're going to go to the shop and we're going to try to look for some wine that will go well with the type of food that we're having.

6
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:16,840
All right.

7
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,720
So we're going to be learning a lot of specific terms.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,120
This is an advanced lesson.

9
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:27,940
So we expect that most of the basics you already know, but some of these more difficult words and phrases are going to be our focus.

10
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,700
So let's take a listen to today's dialogue.

11
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:35,630
Hello there.

12
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:36,730
Welcome to Wine World.

13
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:38,950
Let me know if I can help you out at all.

14
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,350
Yes, please.

15
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:41,570
I could really use some help.

16
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:45,670
I'm going over to my boss's house for dinner tonight and I don't know what kind of wine I should bring.

17
00:00:45,910 --> 00:00:46,290
Okay.

18
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:49,610
Do you know what kind of food will be served?

19
00:00:50,010 --> 00:00:51,270
Well, his wife is Japanese.

20
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,370
He said she makes really good sushi.

21
00:00:54,310 --> 00:00:56,650
That's a bit of a challenge.

22
00:00:57,430 --> 00:01:00,370
Sushi is notoriously difficult to pair with wine.

23
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:02,070
Well, let's see.

24
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:05,700
It'll have to be a white wine, of course.

25
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:06,720
Why?

26
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,140
Wouldn't a red wine go well with sushi?

27
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,700
No, I don't think so.

28
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:15,880
Sushi is a very delicately flavored food and red wine would be a jarring contrast.

29
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:20,320
You need a white wine which has more subtle flavors to complement the fish.

30
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:21,560
I see.

31
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,420
So I should get a bottle of Chardonnay.

32
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:24,420
That's a white wine, right?

33
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:29,560
Yes, Chardonnay is a white wine, but I'm not sure it'd be your best bet.

34
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:35,640
Chardonnay is one of the more full-bodied whites and tends to be a bit oaky.

35
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:40,070
I'd suggest you go for something brighter like this Sauvignon Blanc from New Zealand.

36
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:42,490
Oh, the Sauvignon Blanc?

37
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:43,390
What's that?

38
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:47,510
That's another varietal or type of grape, just like Chardonnay.

39
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:48,250
Let's see.

40
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,190
The label says it's got attractive citrus and grassy aromas that give way to crisp mineral flavors and a bone-dry finish.

41
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,040
Serve chilled.

42
00:01:57,250 --> 00:01:59,190
Oh no, how long will it take to chill the wine?

43
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,880
I'm on my way to dinner now.

44
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,280
Oh, it's okay, don't worry.

45
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:04,300
We'll just choose a wine from the cooler.

46
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,750
We don't have quite as extensive a selection over here, but this Rhone Valley White would be lovely.

47
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:13,730
All right, what varietal is that?

48
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:18,970
Well, this is a French wine, so they don't always specify the varietal on the label.

49
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:25,710
The French believe that the soil a grape is grown in is one of the most important factors in the final flavor of the wine.

50
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:32,270
This wine is probably a blend of a few different types of grapes, mostly Viognier, I'd guess.

51
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,050
And you think this is a good wine?

52
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,950
Yes, this is one of our best sellers.

53
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:42,220
It's not quite as dry as the Sauvignon Blanc we were looking at earlier, which means it's more approachable.

54
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:45,380
It's light and crisp with a bit of a vanilla aroma.

55
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:47,040
Perfect, I'll take it.

56
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:51,640
All right, we're back.

57
00:02:51,920 --> 00:03:02,120
So now we're talking about wines, and one of the first things that really pop up is when we're talking about sushi and how we're trying to get a wine to go well with sushi.

58
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:05,560
All right, so the phrase here was to pair with wine.

59
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:09,320
So sushi is notoriously difficult to pair with wine.

60
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:16,380
All right, so when you talk about wine, you talk about pairing it with food, P-A-I-R, to pair.

61
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:17,540
That's right.

62
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:26,660
So for example, if you're having meat or poultry or chicken, you try to pair it with a wine so basically that the flavors go well together.

63
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:35,560
So commonly we say that red wine pairs well with red meat, or fish and white wine pair well together.

64
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:40,240
So you're pairing these two things means you're using them in the same meal.

65
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:41,280
That's right.

66
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,080
Okay.

67
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:48,760
So when we're talking about pairing a wine with sushi, the girl said, well, what about red wine?

68
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,080
Wouldn't that pair well with sushi?

69
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:55,140
And the attendant said, no, the red wine would be a jarring contrast.

70
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,280
So first of all, we have this word jarring.

71
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:04,640
Something is jarring if it's loud, shocking, abrasive, difficult, annoying.

72
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:06,520
So something that's jarring is loud.

73
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:10,890
And a contrast is something that shows the differences in something.

74
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:11,530
That's right.

75
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:18,150
So when we're saying that it would be a jarring contrast to have sushi with red wine, we're saying that they're just too different.

76
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:22,010
Sushi is too different from the red wine flavor, so they wouldn't go well together.

77
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,360
That's right.

78
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:26,920
And since jarring means it's a bad thing, we think the flavor will be wrong.

79
00:04:27,270 --> 00:04:27,670
It'll be bad.

80
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,490
So we need to look for something else.

81
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:35,270
And the salesperson suggested a wine that has more subtle flavors, white wine.

82
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:36,240
That's right.

83
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:42,360
So this word subtle is actually spelled S-U-B-T-L-E, but the B is silent.

84
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:43,100
That's right.

85
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:44,440
So we say subtle.

86
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:49,120
And it's actually great because it's kind of like the opposite of jarring.

87
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,480
Something that's not jarring is subtle.

88
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,640
Right.

89
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:59,160
So it's a little bit more, I don't know, like relaxed, like not as loud.

90
00:04:59,160 --> 00:04:59,960
It's not obvious.

91
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:03,180
You have to really think about it and look for it.

92
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,100
Something that's subtle is not obvious.

93
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:05,940
That's right.

94
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,920
And now we're talking about one specific type of white wine.

95
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,200
We have a Chardonnay.

96
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:12,160
All right.

97
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:17,780
So we know that there are many, many different kinds of wine out there, but there are some very common ones.

98
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,580
And Chardonnay is one of those.

99
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:23,280
I think Chardonnay tends to be a bit fruitier.

100
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,390
Australia has some famous Chardonnays.

101
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,570
California has some famous Chardonnays.

102
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:30,170
Just remember that Chardonnay is a kind of white wine.

103
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,840
That's right.

104
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:37,970
And one of the ways that they used it to describe Chardonnay is that it's one of the more full-bodied whites.

105
00:05:38,850 --> 00:05:39,070
All right.

106
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:43,080
So whites here, we're talking about white wines, but something that's full-bodied.

107
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:43,730
What does that mean, Marco?

108
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:51,370
So if a wine is full-bodied, it means that it has a little bit of a stronger flavor, like it's a more complete flavor.

109
00:05:51,650 --> 00:05:52,490
It's not as subtle.

110
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:53,160
All right.

111
00:05:53,760 --> 00:06:02,640
So we know that white wines are a bit more subtle than red wines in this case, but within white wines, you can have one that's very full-bodied.

112
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,900
So this is a great phrase for describing wine.

113
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:12,540
We don't really talk about other things being full-bodied, but wine can be full-bodied if it really has what you say, Marco, this big full taste, a bright taste.

114
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,120
That's right.

115
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:23,600
And actually the sales attendant suggested that, well, since the Chardonnay is too or is more full-bodied, then he would recommend maybe a Sauvignon Blanc.

116
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,170
All right.

117
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,190
So Sauvignon Blanc.

118
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:29,390
Blanc is the French word for white, but we use this all the time in English.

119
00:06:29,770 --> 00:06:31,550
Sauvignon Blanc being the kind of wine.

120
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:33,050
Again, it's a white wine.

121
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:37,800
And it's a bit brighter than the Chardonnay.

122
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:38,870
That's what the salesperson said.

123
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,360
That's right.

124
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:50,380
And when we're talking about wines, either red wines or white wines, the way to describe it or the different varieties is actually a varietal of the wines or the type of grape.

125
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:51,260
Right.

126
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:52,920
So varietal.

127
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,720
So you think of variety, varietal.

128
00:06:55,340 --> 00:07:02,300
Varietal is a specific wine word that we use to describe the kind of grape that go into a wine.

129
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:05,480
So we know wine generally comes from grapes.

130
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,400
They're crushed down.

131
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,280
And then the alcohol comes from all the sugars.

132
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,680
But each different kind of grape has a different flavor.

133
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,120
And that's the varietal, the kind of grape.

134
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:15,760
That's right.

135
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:19,320
So just think of it as the variety of the wines that you have.

136
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:21,320
And it's a word used specifically for wines.

137
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:33,140
And well, when the attendant kept talking about the wines and the types of wines they have there, he mentioned that they have a small selection in the refrigerator or in the cooler.

138
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:37,980
So selection in this case means what the store has to offer.

139
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,860
It means all the wines that they sell.

140
00:07:40,790 --> 00:07:46,350
So maybe if you have an extensive selection, it means you have many, many, many different kinds to choose from.

141
00:07:46,830 --> 00:07:53,090
But if you don't have an extensive selection, you have very few wines, that means that you have fewer things to sell.

142
00:07:53,570 --> 00:07:54,110
That's right.

143
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:58,990
So a wide selection of wines or a small selection of wines.

144
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:06,830
And lastly, talking about varietals, we also have what we call a blend, a blend of a few different types of grapes.

145
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Right.

146
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,230
So you can have blends of different things.

147
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:14,010
But in terms of wine, we're talking about using different grapes together to make one wine.

148
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,040
All right.

149
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:18,830
So this is something that's pretty common and it's a way to achieve different flavors.

150
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:19,630
That's right.

151
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:20,630
So a blend.

152
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,170
You also talk about it in, I think, whiskeys.

153
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,670
You have blended whiskeys.

154
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,240
That's right.

155
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:34,790
You can have a single malt, which is one grain in one barrel, or you can have a blend, which would be different grains fermented in different barrels mixed together later.

156
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,280
Okay.

157
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,970
So a lot of great stuff here all about wines.

158
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:41,480
Let's listen to this dialogue one last time.

159
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:45,900
Hello there.

160
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:46,960
Welcome to Wine World.

161
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:49,240
Let me know if I can help you out at all.

162
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:50,560
Yes, please.

163
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:51,820
I could really use some help.

164
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:55,880
I'm going over to my boss's house for dinner tonight and I don't know what kind of wine I should bring.

165
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,360
Okay.

166
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,820
Do you know what kind of food will be served?

167
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,240
Well, his wife is Japanese.

168
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:05,880
He said she makes really good sushi.

169
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:06,820
That's a bit of a challenge.

170
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,460
Sushi is notoriously difficult to pair with wine.

171
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:12,260
Well, let's see.

172
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:15,860
It'll have to be a white wine, of course.

173
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:18,300
Why wouldn't a red wine go well with sushi?

174
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:20,820
No, I don't think so.

175
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:26,020
Sushi is a very delicately flavored food and red wine would be a jarring contrast.

176
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:30,400
You need a white wine which has more subtle flavors to complement the fish.

177
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:31,700
I see.

178
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,880
So I should get a bottle of Chardonnay.

179
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:34,580
That's a white wine, right?

180
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:39,700
Yes, Chardonnay is a white wine, but I'm not sure it'd be your best bet.

181
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:44,820
Chardonnay is one of the more full-bodied whites and tends to be a bit oaky.

182
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:50,200
I'd suggest you go for something brighter like this Sauvignon Blanc from New Zealand.

183
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:52,640
Oh, the Sauvignon Blanc?

184
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:53,540
What's that?

185
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:57,640
That's another varietal or type of grape, just like Chardonnay.

186
00:09:57,940 --> 00:09:58,400
Let's see.

187
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:05,280
The label says it's got attractive citrus and grassy aromas that give way to crisp mineral flavors and a bone-dry finish.

188
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,200
Serve chilled.

189
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:09,300
Oh no, how long will it take to chill the wine?

190
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,040
I'm on my way to dinner now.

191
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:11,820
Oh, it's okay.

192
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:12,400
Don't worry.

193
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,420
We'll just choose a wine from the cooler.

194
00:10:15,050 --> 00:10:21,890
We don't have quite as extensive a selection over here, but this Rhone Valley White would be lovely.

195
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,480
All right, what varietal is that?

196
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:29,090
Well, this is a French wine, so they don't always specify the varietal on the label.

197
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:35,870
The French believe that the soil a grape is grown in is one of the most important factors in the final flavor of the wine.

198
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:42,390
This wine is probably a blend of a few different types of grapes, mostly Viognier, I'd guess.

199
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,190
And you think this is a good wine?

200
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,070
Yes, this is one of our best sellers.

201
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:52,350
It's not quite as dry as the Sauvignon Blanc we were looking at earlier, which means it's more approachable.

202
00:10:52,790 --> 00:10:55,550
It's light and crisp with a bit of a vanilla aroma.

203
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:56,450
Perfect.

204
00:10:56,770 --> 00:10:57,190
I'll take it.

205
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:06,130
All right, so obviously there are a lot more varietals out there.

206
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:09,560
We only talked about two types of wines.

207
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,600
We had a Chardonnay and a Sauvignon Blanc.

208
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,600
That's right.

209
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,790
And the only wines we talked about were white wines.

210
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,810
Of course, there's a whole world of red wines out there.

211
00:11:17,030 --> 00:11:21,390
And then between red and white, you have rosé, which are those pink wines.

212
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:22,550
Those pink wines, yeah.

213
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:32,400
But actually, it's interesting because the culture of drinking wine is not as extensive as we think it is.

214
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:35,310
In many parts of the world, they're not really used to drinking wine.

215
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:36,270
That's right.

216
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:48,400
But then you go to places like France and Italy and South America, like Argentina, Chile, and you experience these different cultures of wine that are quite, I think, quite interesting because they're so different.

217
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:49,200
Yeah, that's right.

218
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:53,040
And it's become even healthy to drink wine.

219
00:11:53,520 --> 00:12:00,360
Medical tests show that if you have one glass of wine with dinner every day, it reduces your chances of heart disease.

220
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,280
That's right.

221
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,340
There's some special ingredient.

222
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:05,960
I'm not sure what it is, but obviously you don't want to drink too much.

223
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:08,020
But if you have a little bit, it's good for your heart.

224
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,840
I think red wine, they say, is good for your heart.

225
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:16,510
So it's interesting, but obviously, maybe in your countries, you don't drink wine or maybe you have a particular type of wine.

226
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:21,170
Like in China, they have, isn't it plum wine or rice wine?

227
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:23,830
Rice wine in China and plum wine, I think, in Japan.

228
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:28,650
So maybe you have a specific type of wine that you want to let us know about.

229
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,150
And of course, if you have any questions or comments, we're always there.

230
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:32,960
Check us out at EnglishPod.com.

231
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:33,960
All right.

232
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:34,960
We'll see you again.

233
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:42,320
Thanks.
